# Week 05 – Kubernetes Basics

## Objective

Learn container orchestration and deployment management.

## Tasks

- [ ] Understand Kubernetes architecture.
- [ ] Install Minikube or use kind for local cluster.
- [ ] Learn about Pods, Services, and Deployments.
- [ ] Create a basic Pod YAML manifest.
- [ ] Deploy an application using a Deployment.
- [ ] Expose the application using a Service.
- [ ] Scale the deployment.
- [ ] Check cluster status with kubectl get nodes.

## Commands

minikube start

kubectl cluster-info

kubectl get nodes

kubectl get pods

kubectl get services

kubectl create deployment my-app --image=nginx

kubectl expose deployment my-app --port=80 --type=NodePort

kubectl scale deployment my-app --replicas=3

kubectl delete deployment my-app

minikube stop

## Deliverable

Running Kubernetes deployment with a exposed service.

## Key Concepts

- Pod: Smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes.
- Service: Exposes a set of Pods as a network service.
- Deployment: Manages replica sets and provides declarative updates.
- Node: A worker machine in the Kubernetes cluster.
- Cluster: A set of nodes managed by Kubernetes.
